.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt TEST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm test ,
.Nd compare and validate values
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar expression
.Pp
.Li \&[
.Ar expression
.Li \&]
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
validates an expression and returns a status code representing its result.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n Ar string
the length of
.Ar string
is nonzero
.It Fl z Ar string
the length of
.Ar string
is zero
.It Ar string
equivalent to
.Fl n Ar string
.It Ar str1 No = Ar str2
the strings are identical.
.It Ar str1 No != Ar str2
the strings are not identical.
.It Ar n1 Fl eq Ar n2
equal.
.It Ar n1 Fl ne Ar n2
not equal.
.It Ar n1 Fl gt Ar n2
greater than.
.It Ar n1 Fl ge Ar n2
greater than or equal.
.It Ar n1 Fl lt Ar n2
less than.
.It Ar n1 Fl le Ar n2
less than or equal.
.It Cm \&! Ar expression
true if
.Ar expression
is false.
.It Fl e Ar file
.Ar file
exists.
.It Fl f Ar file
.Ar file
is a regular file.
.It Fl d Ar file
.Ar file
is a directory.
.It Fl s Ar file
.Ar file
exists and is not empty.
.It Fl r Ar file
.Ar file
is readable.
.It Fl w Ar file
.Ar file
is writable.
.It Fl x Ar file
.Ar file
is executable, or searchable if it is a directory.
.It Fl h Ar file , Fl L Ar file
.Ar file
is a symbolic link.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
